{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789397647,"nonce":"p4N2idX0PEEy8fiYdKddbQhDVJw=","title":"Python: a function returning a generator is lowered as one","message":"A plain function whose return is a generator, `def wrap(i): return\nthree(i)` or a method `def get(self): return self.g`, is typed\n`Ty::Gen` by return inference (`sig.ret` for a call to a generator\nfunction or a generator expression) and then lowered as a generator\nfunction itself: \"Error: a value returned from a generator is not\nsupported yet\".\n\nOnly a body that yields is a generator (`types::is_generator`); the\nreturn type of a function returning one should be `Ty::Gen` for the\nvalue while `is_generator` stays false, and call lowering should start\na fiber only for callees whose body yields. The `for` and draining\nsites that free a fresh generator (`is_generator_start`) already test\nthe expression rather than the type, so they stay right once such a\ncall is a plain call.","files":null}]}